  "description": "An iridescent liquid sea that the music physically drives. A Swift-Hohenberg simulation of parametrically-driven surface waves (Faraday waves) runs on the GPU each frame and is ray-marched as a liquid heightfield: loudness crossing the Faraday THRESHOLD is a real supercritical bifurcation, so the sea is glassy and still below it and erupts into cells above it, and timbre selects the cell size. Colour is thin-film interference off the wave itself, not a palette \u2014 the standing wave IS the film thickness, so the hues ripple and swap as the pattern moves. Sibling to Cymatic Resonance: sound causes the image. Ported physics (FA #73): Swift & Hohenberg 1977, Chen & Vinals 1997.",
